---
/**
 * "Simulators". Name the technology — 42% of the segment names none, and GolfZon,
 * TrackMan and Full Swing are search terms with real credibility weight
 * (playbook-core.md §8, playbook-sim-venue.md §4).
 *
 * ⚠️ NX vs TwoVision is contradicted across the client's own live pages and this
 * is the single most consequential fact on the site.
 *   - Current pages (homepage, /stillwater) say "GolfZon".
 *   - /home-old, /home-2 and /news/golfzon-twovision — all still live, all still
 *     indexed — say "6 GolfZon TwoVision simulators".
 *   - AI-generated search summaries are repeating the TwoVision claim today,
 *     i.e. the site is actively teaching answer engines a fact that may be false
 *     (seo-map.md §0).
 * This page publishes NX because that is what the current pages say, but the
 * claim MUST be confirmed with the client before launch, along with whether and
 * when Lakeville was re-fitted. Everything downstream — schema, titles, the
 * homepage hero — inherits this answer.
 *
 * ⚠️ Also unconfirmed: the "240+ courses" figure appears ONLY on the retired
 * homepages and is not repeated on the current site, so it is stubbed rather
 * than republished.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookButton from '../components/venue/BookButton.astro';
import { getVenues, venuePath } from '../lib/venues';

const venues = await getVenues();

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'GolfZon Simulator Bays — Lakeville & Stillwater MN',
  metaDescription:
    'Six GolfZon bays in Lakeville, four in Stillwater MN — moving swing plate, auto tee-up, real ball flight. Five of six bays suit lefties.',
};

/**
 * What the hardware actually does, described for someone who has never used one.
 *
 * The four titles are the client's own homepage feature bullets, verbatim. The
 * bodies are constrained to what GolfZon publishes about its own sensors
 * (golfzongolf.com/global/user/technology/sensors.do), because this is the one
 * paragraph on the site whose whole job is to sound like it knows the machine:
 *   - the sensors are "positioned above and in FRONT of the player" and "meet at
 *     90 degrees" — not "above and beside you", which is what this said before;
 *   - BALL data (speed, direction and trajectory, spin rate, launch angle, spin
 *     axis) comes from the T2, which is FLOOR-mounted and is not a camera;
 *   - CLUB data (club path, angle of attack, club face impact area) comes from
 *     the overhead TwoVision unit;
 *   - GolfZon publishes "club face impact area", NOT "face angle". Do not put
 *     "face angle" back — it is not a metric they claim.
 * The plate detail ("five-segment", fairway/rough/bunker mats) is likewise
 * GolfZon's own, and replaced an invented "in a bunker shot it drops".
 * See truth-audit.md §C6 and §U19.
 */
const hardware = [
  [
    'A moving swing plate',
    'The floor you stand on tilts to match the lie. GolfZon builds it in five segments — one under the ball, four under your stance — with fairway, rough and bunker mats. That is the part people do not expect, and it is why the ball behaves like it does outdoors rather than like a video game.',
  ],
  [
    'High-speed camera sensors',
    'The cameras sit above and in front of you, angled at each other, and read the club: the path it takes, how steeply it comes into the ball, and where on the face you hit it. A separate sensor in the floor reads the ball — speed, launch angle, spin rate and spin axis. Nothing is attached to you and nothing is attached to the club.',
  ],
  [
    'Auto tee-up and ball return',
    'The machine tees the next ball for you. You do not bend down between shots, and you do not run out of balls — they are included, you never bring your own.',
  ],
  [
    'A touchscreen next to you',
    'You pick the course and the settings from the screen in the bay, and it scores the round for you. Staff set it up on your first visit; you do not need to know anything going in.',
  ],
];

/** Practice and play are different products in the same bay. */
const modes = [
  [
    'Play a course',
    'Eighteen holes on a real course, rendered hole by hole. Budget about an hour per person — four of you in one bay is roughly a four-hour round, which is why most groups play nine or split across two bays.',
  ],
  [
    'Practise',
    'A driving range and a putting green with no queue, no weather and no lost balls. Every shot comes back with numbers, which is the point — you find out what your 7-iron actually carries instead of what you tell people it carries.',
  ],
  [
    'Play a game',
    'Closest-to-the-pin, longest drive, and the arcade-style formats. This is what a group who do not really golf ends up playing, and it is fine.',
  ],
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold lg:text-5xl">The bays</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-inkMuted">
      Ten <strong>GolfZon</strong> simulator bays across two venues. You hit a real ball with a real club into a screen, the
      cameras read what happened, and the floor under you tilts to match the lie. Nothing is strapped to you and nothing needs
      setting up.
    </p>

    {/* 1. Per venue, with the numbers a golfer actually screens on. */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">What is where</h2>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          venues.map((venue) => (
            <li class="rounded border-2 border-ink/15 p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">
                <a href={venuePath(venue)} class="hover:underline">
                  {venue.data.name}
                </a>
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-inkMuted">
                {venue.data.bays} bays · {venue.data.simulator}
              </p>
              {venue.data.intro && <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">{venue.data.intro}</p>}
              <div class="mt-6">
                <BookButton venue={venue} size="sm" variant="outline" />
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <dl class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold">Left-handed players</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-inkMuted">
            Five of the six Lakeville bays are set up for both right and left handers. One is right-handed only, so if
            you are a lefty in a group of six, say so when you book.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold">Clubs and balls</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-inkMuted">
            Balls are included — every bay has its own. Bring your own clubs if you have them; rental sets are $15 at
            Lakeville and they are basic, not fitted.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold">How many in a bay</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-inkMuted">
            Up to six people, though four is the number that keeps a round moving. Lakeville seats up to 36 golfers
            across all six bays.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold">Screens</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-inkMuted">Nine TVs at Lakeville, so whatever is on is on while you play.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <p class="mt-6 rounded border-2 border-dashed border-ink/25 p-4 text-sm text-inkMuted">
        <strong>STUB —</strong> the Stillwater equivalents are unknown: how many of the four bays play left-handed, the TV
        count, seating, whether club rental is available there, and whether it is $15. A left-handed golfer in Stillwater
        currently cannot find out whether they can play at all.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* 2. The technology, named and explained. */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">What GolfZon does</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        GolfZon is the system in our bays. Around the Twin Cities you will also see TrackMan and Full Swing. Four things
        separate it from hitting into a net.
      </p>
      <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          hardware.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="text-lg font-semibold">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-inkMuted">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <p class="mt-8 rounded border-2 border-dashed border-ink/25 p-4 text-sm text-inkMuted">
        <strong>STUB — confirm before launch.</strong> The current site says GolfZon; three older pages that are still live
        say GolfZon TwoVision, and third-party directories and AI search summaries are repeating TwoVision today. We need
        a straight answer on which system is in the Lakeville bays and, if it was re-fitted, when. This is the single most
        consequential unconfirmed fact on the site.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* 3. What you can do with it. Practice vs play, per the spec. */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Practice, play, or just mess about</h2>
      <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          modes.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="text-lg font-semibold">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-inkMuted">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <p class="mt-8 rounded border-2 border-dashed border-ink/25 p-4 text-sm text-inkMuted">
        <strong>STUB —</strong> the course list. A "240+ courses and 6 arcade games" figure exists only on two retired homepages
        and is not repeated on the current site, so it is not republished here. We need the current course count and, ideally,
        five or six named courses people would recognise — that is what the golfer comparing venues is looking for.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* 4. Never used one. The largest addressable market (playbook-core.md §8). */}
    <section class="mt-section rounded bg-surface p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Never used one?</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        Staff start the bay for you and show you the screen. Turn the difficulty down, turn the wind off, and take as
        many shots as you like — there is no group behind you and the bay is yours for the hour. If you top one, the
        machine tees another ball up.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        You do not need clubs, you do not need shoes, and you do not need to know the rules.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* Every page ends in a transactional CTA (playbook-core.md §6). */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Try one</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        A bay is $35 an hour through 30 September 2026 — per bay, not per person, up to six of you.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <BookButton size="lg" />
        <a href="/rates/" class="inline-block rounded border-2 border-current px-8 py-4 font-semibold hover:bg-ink/5">
          See rates &amp; hours
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
